      "message": "There\u0027s a lot of conditional logic in this test, which is against best practice for unit tests.  You should aim for tests to be short, tight, and clear; for example, rather than looping over the error messages here and dynamically handling them separately, this test should know precisely what it expects to break.  When I read this code I wondered to myself \"what\u0027s wrong with the shader he\u0027s testing?\" and then when I looked at the shader code, the error doesn\u0027t leap out at me.\n\nSo rather than loops and if() branches to cover multiple behaviors in a single test, try to write multiple shorter tests where each test tests a specfic behavior and only that behavior.",
